## Package comparison

The round-1 phase package remains aligned with approved Phase 1, and this rework stays within its file scope.

## Findings

### Critical — The Effect-owned daemon architecture remains unimplemented

The request decoder now uses schema outputs, but the defining runtime issue is unchanged. `provider.ts`, `server.ts`, `client.ts`, and `music-sessiond.ts` still contain no Effect services, layers, scopes, fibers, or streams. The coordinator’s `Queue` and `SubscriptionRef`s are isolated values manipulated through `Effect.runSync` inside a Promise/class lifecycle; callback sets still provide replay, an async method still drives commands, and raw `setTimeout` still drives polling/reconciliation. There is no `Schedule`/`TestClock` and no daemon scope that can interrupt active provider/socket work and run finalizers. This does not satisfy the phase intent or exact implementation steps.

### High — The required tagged Effect error boundary is still absent

Internal failures remain plain objects and string-prefixed JavaScript `Error`s. `server.ts` still decides whether a command failed with `SERVER_BUSY`, `DISPOSED`, or `PROVIDER_FAILURE` by parsing the error message prefix. The phase explicitly requires schema-tagged Effect errors internally, interruption preservation, and one mapping to stable wire errors at the boundary. Request decoding is improved, but the error model remains unimplemented.

### High — Phase 1 acceptance remains largely unsupported by tests

The session suite remains nine tests and still lacks required coverage for late-subscriber status/state replay, incompatible hello and capability negotiation, duplicate/out-of-order response handling, malformed/oversized third-client isolation, stale sample rejection, coalesced sampling, 3/5/8 scheduling under `TestClock`, queue overflow and continuation after provider failure, optimistic seek, reconciliation timing, disconnect/indeterminate commands, listener isolation, and exact-once scoped finalization. The Effect queue/ref behavior and terminal client behavior have no direct tests. The coder result also continues to substitute `npm pack ./packages/music-core --dry-run` for the exact verify command, which has not passed as written.
